{"availability":"available","full":"MarwaneHosni/CSSDirect","name":"CSSDirect","description":"♾️ Learn CSS by building it: drag components, apply live CSS, get graded by a real validation engine. ","category":"Design","language":null,"stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-21T17:43:06Z","updated":"2026-08-21T17:45:11Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://cssdirect.vercel.app/","topics":["accessibility","css","css-learning","drag-and-drop","edtech","education","frontend","gamification","interactive-learning","javascript","react","sandbox","tailwindcss","vite","webapp","zustand"],"demo":"https://cssdirect.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:33.117Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:33.117Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:33.117Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T03:24:33.117Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An interactive CSS learning tool that teaches layout by building it — drag components, apply real CSS properties, and watch live style changes. No code editor required.","This is a documentation-only showcase repository. It describes a real, working application — its architecture, features, and engineering decisions — without including the application's source code. The source lives in a separate private repository.","CSS Direct is a local-first, offline-capable web application for learning CSS by doing. Instead of reading property definitions or watching videos, learners work in a real sandbox: drag one of 20 realistic UI components (button, navbar, modal, pricing card…) onto a canvas, drag a CSS property onto it, pick a value, and see the computed result applied live."],"features":["Sandbox — free-form exploration. No lesson, no goal; just build and experiment. Composers can resize, reorder layers, compare before/after states, preview at multiple breakpoints, and export the final CSS.","Guided lessons — a step engine validates the learner's actual canvas against the current step using a composable check engine (11 check types with logical combinators), gives targeted hints on miss, applies…","Challenges — procedurally generated exercises from 6 templates, with difficulty scaling and a grade breakdown.","Interactive CSS validation — lessons don't compare strings; they run a predicate-style check engine against the live scene (element selected, property applied, computed style matched, layout matched, element counts…),…","A real design tool, not a demo — the canvas is a miniature editor: scene tree, layers, selection, resize handles with alignment guides, undo/redo with style snapshots, responsive previews, and CSS/JSON export."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MarwaneHosni/CSSDirect/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b21f8e5f010a638acd8de1e6d8ae985626eda71214729ffb24aedee2f5c97a99","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:33.217Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:33.217Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An interactive CSS learning tool that teaches layout by building it — drag components, apply real CSS properties, and watch live style changes. No code editor required.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MarwaneHosni/CSSDirect/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"No accounts, no servers, no data held by the product.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MarwaneHosni/CSSDirect/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"optional","text":"Sync — optional GitHub Gist adapter (personal access token)","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MarwaneHosni/CSSDirect/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"b21f8e5f010a638acd8de1e6d8ae985626eda71214729ffb24aedee2f5c97a99","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MarwaneHosni/CSSDirect/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:33.218Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-21T17:45:11Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MarwaneHosni/CSSDirect/blob/